{
  "id": "0199897e6530-705449069bac58399c92f603",
  "section": "Math",
  "domain": "Advanced Math",
  "related_skills": [
    "Linear functions",
    "Nonlinear functions"
  ],
  "unit": "Unit 13 - Functions",
  "description": "Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 13 - Functions for SAT Math preparation.",
  "duration": 45,
  "content": "<ul>\n<li>Each <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> has only <strong>one</strong> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></math>.  </li>\n<li>You cannot have two outputs for the same input.  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example 1</strong><br />\nIs this a function?<br />\n- <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> → Yes (every input unique).<br />\n- <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> → No (input 1 has two outputs).  </p>\n<hr />\n\n<ul>\n<li>Division by zero is not allowed.  </li>\n<li>Square roots of negatives are not real.  </li>\n<li>Logarithms of nonpositive numbers are undefined.  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example 2</strong>  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>\n<p>is undefined at \n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math></p>\n<p>.  </p>\n<p><strong>Example 3</strong>  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math>\n<p>is undefined if \n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math></p>\n<p>.  </p>\n<hr />\n\n<p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> are functions, then:  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>&#x02218;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>\n\n<p><strong>Example 4</strong><br />\nIf <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>, find <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>&#x02218;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>&#x02218;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<hr />\n\n<p>Solve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p><strong>Example 5</strong><br />\nIf <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>, solve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>9</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>&#x000B1;</mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>\n\n<hr />\n\n<ul>\n<li>Vertical Line Test: If a vertical line crosses graph more than once → not a function.  </li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example 6</strong><br />\n- <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math> → function (parabola passes test).<br />\n- Circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> → not a function (fails vertical line test).  </p>\n<hr />\n\n<ul>\n<li>Watch for <strong>undefined values</strong>.  </li>\n<li>Composition is a common SAT trick.  </li>\n<li>Always check if graphs pass vertical line test.  </li>\n<li>Solutions to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></math> mean <strong>x-values where graph crosses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></math></strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n\n<p>1) Is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math> a function? Why or why not?<br />\n2) For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></math>, where is it undefined?<br />\n3) If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>, find <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>&#x02218;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.<br />\n4) Solve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></math> when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math>.<br />\n5) Does the graph of a sideways parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math> represent a function?  </p>\n<hr />\n\n<p>1) Yes, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math> is a function since each input has only one output (though domain is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>).  </p>\n<p>2) Denominator <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>, so undefined there.  </p>\n<p>3) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>&#x02218;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>. So <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>4) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>8</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mspace width=\"1em\" /><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>5) No, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math> fails vertical line test (two <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></math> for each <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>).  </p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-python\">\n</code></pre>",
